          "date": "2026-11-04 01:39:42.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-21061 llapi: keep new dirs of a migrated tree in the pool",
        "message": "LU-21061 llapi: keep new dirs of a migrated tree in the pool\n\nAfter \"lfs migrate -m -p POOL DIRECTORY\", new subdirectories of\nDIRECTORY can still be created outside the pool.  The MDTs set POOL\nonly in the default directory layout of a plain directory they move,\nso DIRECTORY keeps its old default when it is already on an MDT of\nthe pool, and loses it when it is migrated to a striped directory.\n\nIn llapi_migrate_mdt(), once the tree is migrated, set POOL in the\ndefault directory layout of DIRECTORY, keeping the rest of it apart\nfrom an MDT index outside the pool, or give it a single stripe on any\nMDT of the pool if it has none.\n\nTest-Parameters: mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=ost-pools\nSigned-off-by: Di Wang <diwa@nvidia.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm\nChange-Id: I6f2a4d5dd16ad40fa7b4d8416e0ed892a45bf2c2\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
